@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed protected request across network/runtime boundaries
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Browser as B
participant "Optional balancer (if adopted)" as L
participant "HTTPS reverse proxy" as P
participant "Trusted application owner" as A
database "Current authority / publication / record state" as DB
participant "Private artifact adapter" as F
alt starting direct ingress candidate
 B -> P : HTTPS intended protected request
else optional balancing alternative
 B -> L : HTTPS intended protected request
 L -> P : evaluated trusted transport / forwarded context
end
P -> A : validated runtime boundary / intended route
A -> DB : resolve current viewer/resource scope + exact representation
DB --> A : versioned eligibility / available identity or refusal
alt permitted current guarded admission
 A -> F : exact scoped usable artifact
 F --> A : permitted delivery context or unavailable
 A --> P : authorized projection / controlled bytes or accurate unavailable
 P --> B : protected response
else denied / stale / missing
 A --> P : safe bounded result; no private fallback
 P --> B : actual denied/unavailable result
end
note over P,F
 Concrete proxy/cache/range and revocation admission rules need evaluated configuration.
 An internal redirect cannot expose raw private paths; already emitted bytes cannot be recalled.
end note
@enduml
